preConditionHook:
// EL: topRun = CountIF((close - low) > threshold * (high - low + epsilon),
// runBars), and the mirror on high - close. CountIF counts bars 0..Length-1
// INCLUDING the current bar and its condition is a true SERIES whose own
// offsets shift per counted bar (EL_FEATURES `countif`, VERIFIED), so the
// unshifted condition counts this bar and the runBars-1 before it. The counted
// condition is on PRICES, which have real history back to the chart start, so
// no zero-filled variable mirror is needed.
//
// The counts are EL numeric variables, kept as doubles, and can never exceed
// runBars -- so el_ge(topRun, runBars) is the all-of-N test without a float
// equality (ExitOnFirstOppositeBodyAfterRun's spelling). Every comparison is an
// EL relational, so el_gt / el_ge carry the tolerance.
//
// PRODUCT FORM, never the quotient CloseRangePosition writes: nothing is
// divided, so a bar whose high equals its low cannot raise EL's runtime
// divide-by-zero. epsilon is that rule's book literal, and in the product form
// its only effect is to make a zero-range bar fail both sides.
//
// The counts are class members and persist across bars, so both are reset.
//
// Deepest bar touched: runBars - 1.
topRun = 0.0;
botRun = 0.0;
for (int i = 0; i < (int)runBars; ++i) {
    if (el_gt(close[i] - low[i], threshold * (high[i] - low[i] + epsilon))) topRun += 1;
    if (el_gt(high[i] - close[i], threshold * (high[i] - low[i] + epsilon))) botRun += 1;
}
